    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (79.32) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), our two strongest plays of the day. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a favorable matchup against Mahle, and despite the slight drag from the opposing backstop, his elite sprint speed remains our primary engine for stolen base production. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a monster outing; a significant 14% boost from both park factors and platoon advantage against Alcantara, combined with his placement in the two-hole, makes him an essential start. **Max Muncy** (70.70) and **Seiya Suzuki** (70.60) also clear the 70-point threshold comfortably, with **Seiya Suzuki** receiving a helpful bump from favorable wind conditions at the park, further elevating his floor against the right-handed Canning.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Jose Caballero**, who fell just short at 45.11. While his stolen base profile is traditionally valuable, a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a difficult platoon matchup against Mize ultimately pushed him into a reserve role in favor of the higher-projected efficiency of **Zach McKinstry** (49.23). We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Cole Young**; while we have projected them in their historical spots, their final scores remain fluid. **Cole Young** (45.50) is currently our most marginal starter, sitting just above our 40-point floor; he remains in the lineup for now, but any downward adjustment to his batting order or a late change to the opposing defensive configuration could lead to a pivot. We continue to hold **Trevor Story** on the IL while maintaining depth with **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Henry Bolte** to weather the remaining grind of the season.",
